## 🎒 Practical Tips for a Smooth Family Trip

| Topic | Advice |
|-------|--------|
| **Transport** | City centre is walkable. For farther spots (Sefton Park, Anfield) use **Merseytravel** buses (routes 10, 26) or a short **Merseyrail** ride. |
| **Weather** | Liverpool can be rainy; pack a lightweight raincoat and waterproof shoes. The indoor attractions (museums, stadium tours) are perfect rain‑day backups. |
| **Tickets** | Book online for the River Mersey Cruise, Anfield tours, and the Beatles bus tours – you’ll get a QR code for fast entry. |
| **Strollers** | All major attractions (Museums, Albert Dock, Sefton Park) are stroller‑friendly. The hop‑on‑hop‑off bus has low‑floor access. |
| **Food** | Most venues offer **Kids’ Menus**. For a quick bite, try the **Baltic Market** (food‑court style) – lots of choices for picky eaters. |
| **Restrooms** | Restrooms are available at Albert Dock, World Museum, and Liverpool ONE. The stadium tours have family‑friendly facilities as well. |
| **Currency** | Prices are shown in GBP; most places accept cards. Some smaller cafés may prefer cash, so keep a few pounds handy. |
| **Accessibility** | Wheelchair‑accessible routes are available on the River Mersey Cruise and most museums. Contact the venue in advance if you need specific assistance. |

